--
^warning: ignoring
--
guess_template_args_template_id ignored A's surplus arguments, so `f(tup<A>)'
deduced A = char from tup<char, char> and was viable through tup's
converting constructor template; for S, the already-instantiated S(tup<int>)
was offered as a candidate and selected the same way.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18
accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
